Fork PR (same branch, for browsing): https://github.com/AlexPerrin/OpenRune-Server/pull/12

Content area from OpenRune/OpenRune-Server#353 (answers there: all of it, one PR per row, ids renumbered against main, wiki data is fine).

From our per-feature patch `30-plank-sack` (in [`openrune/upstream/`](https://github.com/AlexPerrin/osrs-plugins-reverse/tree/main/openrune/upstream) of osrs-plugins-reverse), on `main` (`1be5dfb5f`).

**Problem.** The plank sack had no Fill, Check or Empty.

**Change.** New module `content/other/plank-sack`:
- Up to 28 planks of the seven types in the `plank_sack_*` varbits RuneLite's Plank Sack plugin reads.
- Fill (or a plank used on the sack), Check ('Oak planks: 3' per type, 'Your sack is currently empty.'), Empty into the inventory.
- A `PlayerItemStorageHook` lets content use planks straight from the sack while it is in the inventory (inventory first).

**Tests.** `PlankSackScriptTest` (3, integration).

On this branch (Docker `eclipse-temurin:21`, upstream's `./gradlew`, 4 GB container; a clean `freshCache` of main restored first, then `:or-cache:buildCache :or-cache:mergePluginGamevals`, then each task as a separate run, then `run` to "Server ready"): buildCache pass, `spotlessCheck` pass, `assemble` pass, `test` pass, `integration` pass, boot pass (Server ready in 8.151531140s). `tools/scripts/fix_gameval_conflicts.py --check` finds no conflicts on this branch, nor with all of our open content PRs merged together.

Nothing was checked in game from this exact branch; the in-game checks above were on our own server build (an older main plus these and our other patches).

**Data sources.** Varbits from the cache; Check wording as RuneLite's Plank Sack plugin parses it (BSD).

**Caveats.**
- Fill/full/no-space messages are best guesses.
- The sawmill does not fill the sack yet.

**Release note.** The plank sack can be filled, checked and emptied, and building can use planks from it.

